# The `work` CLI — the verb map

`work` is the single Workbooks command line — **author · build · run · deploy · operate**. It runs the
same binary natively on your machine AND inside the WASM agent sandbox, so an agent has the exact tools
a human does. It operates on a folder of `.work` source: it weaves the tree into one shippable workbook
and stands up a **nexus** to run it.

**When to use:** whenever you need to know which `work` command does what — before authoring, deploying,
or driving a nexus/cloud from the terminal.

## The verbs (source of truth: `cli/src/main.zig`)

**Author — read & verify `.work` trees (local)**
- `work check [dir]` — resolve references + audit capabilities.
- `work structure [dir]` — list the units in the tree.
- `work why | near | wit :unit` — code-graph deps + the generated WIT world.
- `work lint` — style / consistency checks.
- `work note` — capture / read notes.

**Build — weave & run**
- `work new <template> [dest]` — scaffold an example project to own + edit.
- `work weave <dir> <out>` — weave a tree into one self-contained artifact.
- `work graph <dir> <out>` — render the code graph as a workbook.
- `work dev <dir>` — watch & re-weave on change (+ nexus hot-swap).

**Deploy — stand up a runtime, local or cloud**
- `work deploy init | validate | apply` — scaffold · check · deploy the `.work` config.
- `work deploy verify | status | down` — health-probe · inspect · tear down a nexus.
- `work secret set | get | list` — secrets in the OS keychain (never in source).

**Cloud — this org's autopoet machine (needs `work login`)**
- `work cloud provision` — stand up / roll this org's cloud brain machine.
- `work cloud machine` — inspect its state + image.
- `work cloud down` — tear it down (storage-only until re-provisioned).

**Agents — drive the nexus's agents (needs `work login`)**
- `work agent ls` — the agent roster on the active nexus.
- `work agent run <name> "<task>"` — run an agent on a brief, print the answer.
- `work runs` — the durable run ledger (the dashboard's Runs view).
- `work env ls | set | rm` — the nexus env / secret store (the dashboard's Secrets).

**Platform — identity, contexts, the control plane**
- `work login <url> --email … --password …` · `work whoami` — authenticate · show identity.
- `work ctx [use <name>]` · `work nexus <url>` — manage/switch targets (the active nexus, local ↔ cloud) ·
  point at an engine. Switching is the `ctx use` subcommand, not a top-level verb.
- `work help` · `work version` — usage · version.

## Key facts
- **Non-interactive by default** — append forced flags (the shell canon); never hang on a prompt.
- The nexus you target is the `work login` / `work use` **active** one — local (`http://localhost:4000`)
  or cloud (`app.workbooks.sh`).
- Some verbs are **privileged in-runtime** — an in-sandbox agent has a narrower surface than a human.
- Builds the WASM sandbox can't host use `mix forge run "<cmd>"` (the Forge micro-VM, LOCAL-ONLY) — that
  is NOT a `work` verb.
